Stop the AWPM Phase2 scans at the end of recvTuples. The loops that walk
the tuples of one column (`std::get<0>(recvTuples[idx1]) == mi`) have no
bounds check, so after the last column they read recvTuples[size()]. That
is out of bounds, and _GLIBCXX_ASSERTIONS aborts on it: STRUMPACK's
SPARSE_mpi_CombBLAS test (matching job 6, GetAWPM) aborted in
CSRMatrixMPI::matching.

diff --git a/Applications/BipartiteMatchings/ApproxWeightPerfectMatching.h b/Applications/BipartiteMatchings/ApproxWeightPerfectMatching.h
index 745558ba..ed4f98c4 100644
--- a/Applications/BipartiteMatchings/ApproxWeightPerfectMatching.h
+++ b/Applications/BipartiteMatchings/ApproxWeightPerfectMatching.h
